-- An unknown is not an absence.
--
-- `Member.joined_at` is declared and nothing here sets it, so reading it runs
-- out of world. Asked either way round, the honest answer is the same one: not
-- that she has no joining date, and not that she has one, but that nothing
-- said. The two steps are separate because an undecided assertion stops the
-- ones after it in its own step, and the point of this fixture is that both
-- directions are undecided rather than one of them.

journey AnUnknownIsNotAnAbsence {
    goal: A declared field nobody set is undecided whichever way it is asked,
          because answering either way states a conclusion nothing reached.

    cast:
        ada: Member

    given:
        ada.name = "Ada"

    1. nobody has said when she joined
        after 1.day
        then ada.joined_at does not exist

    2. and asking the other way round does not settle it either
        after 1.day
        then ada.joined_at exists

    ends: Neither question was answered, and both said so.
}
